      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "The reference class comprises twelve consecutive original-period Arkansas prints from July 2025 through June 2026. Their mean base rate is 74.3333%. The latest three average 71.3333%, and June is 72%. A persistence prior anchored on June reflects the recent lower level. The single July-to-August 2025 increase from 74% to 75% is insufficient to estimate a seasonal adjustment."
      },
      {
        "kind": "text",
        "text": "Level, momentum, one-off and policy effects are treated separately. The level update takes the twelve-print mean down 2.3333 percentage points to June's 72%. April, May and June show stabilization rather than a continuing large decline, so momentum adjustment is zero. No quantified August-specific one-off or policy adjustment is supported by the fetched sources. CMS notes that renewal cohort composition and how renewals completed after forms are sent are classified can affect ex parte reporting."
      },
      {
